.TH TUTOR 1
.SH NAME
tutor \- CAI/PLATO-style branching-lesson engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/tutor
.RI [ lesson-file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tutor
is a work-alike of the CAI (computer-assisted instruction)/PLATO
chapter of Nelson's
.IR "Computer Lib/Dream Machines" :
a lesson the student's own typed answers steer, not a document they
just read \(em distinct from this system's static
.B !Lessons
reading material (a pinboard folder of plain documents), which has no
judging or branching at all.
.PP
.I Lesson-file
defaults to
.BR /lib/tutor/intro.tt .
A lesson is a graph of named frames; each frame shows its text, takes
a typed answer, and judges it against an ordered list of keyword
rules (the first case-insensitive substring match wins), branching to
a named next frame, with a
.B DEFAULT
fallback if nothing matches. A running score of correct answers out
of attempts is kept in the toolbar.
.PP
The plain-text lesson format:
.IP
.nf
.ft L
LESSON <title>
START <framename>

FRAME <name>
TEXT
<one or more lines, shown verbatim>
END
JUDGE <keyword> <correct 0|1> <next> <response text...>
...
DEFAULT <correct 0|1> <next> <response text...>
.ft
.fi
.PP
Blank lines between frames are ignored; JUDGE rules are tried in
order, and DEFAULT is used when none match.
.SH FILES
.TF /lib/tutor/intro.tt
.TP
.B /lib/tutor/intro.tt
The default sample lesson, covering the Dis virtual machine and the
Limbo language.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/tutor.b
.br
.B /appl/lib/tutor.b
.br
